<<~ aka "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/RFC-2119#/normative-language">>

<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Braided Islands

''Several causal islands run in parallel, braided into one working only through carried text.''
No island reads another's log; no island holds authority over another; the braid coheres at the
loom — the hands that carry — never in shared state.

''The pattern scales'' (ruled 2026-08-15): AI sessions braided by an operator · human-human
dyads · human-self and human-environment. An island names any sovereign log-holder; the laws
below read the same at every scale. Where the ''worker swarm'' spawns spirits that execute and
dissolve, the braid stands ''peers that persist''. First enactment: Session 0.1, three islands.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/laws>>

!! The Laws

''Precedence inversion.'' Each island declares an ordered duty-pair, and the orders differ by
design — same capabilities, different stacks, no duty uncovered. ''At most ONE island speaks
events; every other island speaks proposals'' — declared in its red, never assumed. A
proposal-island's output rides Provisional until a hand carries it into the event-island's world.

''The loom.'' One operator holds the input gate and runs the islands; others reach the system
through the operator's curation. A narrow gate reads more pono early — sync pressure belongs in
dev work, not live sessions. A braid without a loom degrades to drift.

''The crossing law.''
# No island reads another's log; the working tree serves no one as a channel.
# Text crosses only in human hands; the carrying hand IS the authorization — arrivals read as
  operator-introduced.
# Dual stamps, never merged: the source's reckoning quoted, the receiver's beside it.
# Write approvals tier: the event-island MAY hold full write; proposal-islands hold their own
  domain and MUST ask for more.
# Sealed content surfaces only through the operator's explicit gate.

''The boot law.'' Each island boots from a ''red'' carrying the grammar in the first input, and
declaring: its precedence stack · its loci · its write scope · its rating law · ''its siblings
by name'' · this crossing law. Reds live as durable memes so a braid re-boots identically.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/degraded-braids>>

!! Degraded-Braid States

* ''Island Fusion'' — attribution collapses across islands (the carrier-pigeon precedent: two
  sessions ferried WITHOUT the chiasmus → self-misnaming within an evening). The per-turn
  session-form URIs stand as anti-fusion infrastructure. //Recover:// halt crossings; re-emit
  aims; re-introduce by name.
* ''Authority Leak'' — a proposal-island narrates as event. //Tell:// past-tense fiction.
  //Recover:// re-mark Provisional; the loom declines to carry the leak.
* ''Ghost Sync'' — an island assumes a sibling knows what no hand carried. //Recover:// ask for
  the crossing; the loom supplies or denies.
* ''Stale Relay'' — action on a superseded crossing. //Recover:// dual stamps make it checkable;
  the newer stamp wins aloud.
* ''Braid Capture'' — one island's register colonizes the others through the relay. //Recover://
  the loom paraphrases for a stretch; each island re-anchors its own register.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/when-to-braid>>

!! When to Braid

Braid when the working needs ''simultaneous incompatible postures'' — one session holding them
all flattens into whichever posture spoke last. Do not braid for scale (spirits serve that), nor
without a loom.

<<~/ahu>>

